that it was a little weird that you have to, you know, press the up button to throw your

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:39.900
sub-weapon, but I also kind of understood it.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:45.060
Yeah. Like, you're going to have to use that stuff, like, to throw a dagger, you're not going to

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:50.020
be able to just be, like, walking and throwing daggers or, like, using the stopwatch and not,

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:52.280
like, thinking about how I'm supposed to be using those things.

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:53.600
So I gave them a pass on that.

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:54.800
I didn't mind it.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:59.580
It's just another constraint of having a small controller.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:02.460
But the sub-weapons themselves are pretty good.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:09.140
I mostly opted for the boomerang, where I could, because if you do it right, you can kind

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:14.340
of get two hits off of the character, because it does kind of extend out further than just

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:17.860
hitting the person. It's kind of weird that it doesn't, like, lodge inside of them or something.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.480
It just goes past them and then comes back around.

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:22.440
I found it the most effective, for me at least.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:27.460
Yeah. I saw, I watched a speed run of it also, because I was curious, and I saw that guy doing stuff

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:33.500
with holy water that was really cool, where he'd throw it down and then have an enemy,

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:34.880
like, chase him.

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:38.440
But he would throw it and then walk through it, and the enemy chasing him would just die

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:39.300
before it got to him.

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:41.720
Okay. By walking into the fire.

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:42.780
By walking into it. Yeah.

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:45.600
So I think there's a lot of cool stuff that you can do with all the weapons.

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:47.320
And so I think it's cool that they each have their own.

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:48.760
Yeah. I mean, even just, like, you know.

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:53.000
Not to jump around too much. Yeah, talking about, like, the axe even, which I thought was real funny.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:56.720
I thought that was, like, a late game item, because the first time I played this game,

00:14:56.780 --> 00:15:01.180
it didn't show up for me until the Grim Reaper stage, where those axe knights are.

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:06.940
Yeah, yeah. So I was like, oh, wow, finally, like, the axe, I can combat them with the axe thing.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:09.180
And I thought it was, like, a really good weapon.

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.140
I wasn't too crazy about it.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:13.680
But one thing I liked about it, just to talk about details,

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:19.560
is that if you throw the axe at the axe knights, and it goes beyond the shield and kind of clips

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.980
them in the head, it does extra damage.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:26.940
It doesn't require, it only requires two to three hits, depending on where it hit them,

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:29.080
as long as it hits them on the back of the head.

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:32.380
Wow, I didn't know that they had sweet spots.

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:33.540
Right, that it matters, yeah.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:37.780
A lot of the enemies in the game have, yeah, have a sweet spot to them,

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:40.100
or a specific sub-weapon that would work on them.

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:42.360
So, like, early Mega Man mechanics, in a way.

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:45.380
Well, that, because now I'm curious as to whether or not this is true,

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:51.800
but do you guys know, are some of these weapons fixed, like, in a spot where you find them?

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:53.060
Or, like, when I played through another?

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:59.200
Some are. Because I felt like I would always, or frequently, end up with the weapon that was the most useful

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:00.680
against the boss I was coming up to.

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:02.500
And I thought that was just good game design.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:04.580
Yeah, I don't know if it's good game design or not.

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:07.640
I will say that, like, yeah, there are definitely some that are planted.

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:13.000
For instance, at the very end, the holy water is always available for you to fight off Dracula.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:17.820
But, like, I can't say with certainty that, like, every single candle is going to have, like,

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:19.520
that specific sub-weapon behind it.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:22.700
You mentioned that you didn't get the axe until the end, which is what made me...

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:24.120
Just on my first playthrough, though.

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:27.240
I did wind up getting it on another playthrough, like, in the first level.

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:33.120
And I was like, oh, this is great, too, because the phantom bat is a good way to take on the axe.

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:36.620
I got the axe for the bat, the cloak, or the clock?

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:39.720
The clock. I'm reading my notes and I read cloak.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:41.900
The clock for Medusa, which was perfect.

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:44.960
Which is perfect, yeah. Because it stops the head in its tracks.

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:48.960
And then the throwing knife for the mummy, which was perfect, because there's two mummies.

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:51.720
So I could throw back and forth and stay between them.

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:52.580
Well, I mean, I don't want to get...

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:54.960
We won't get into the bosses too much right now.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:17:02.020
But the stopwatch is interesting, because the stopwatch actually stops time, but requires more hearts.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:05.140
Yeah. Right. So it's like a good trade-off.

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:07.000
I was wondering why I wouldn't work with one heart.

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:11.140
Yeah. It was something I thought was, like, you know, I was like, oh, this might be kind of broken.

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:15.600
Like, you know, I could just stop time whenever I want, but then you quickly run out of those hearts.

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:20.920
Yeah. One thing I will say about going back to just placement of these items and where they drop,

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:25.940
I do know just because I looked at a couple strategy guides that there are some that will

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:31.700
always drop the dagger or will always drop some other specific item.

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:32.740
Well, then that's good game design.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:33.720
Yeah, that's good game design.

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:43.380
Another thing is that if you have died and, like, if you come into a level pretty, like, powered up,

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:48.880
like you've gotten your whip upgrades, there will be some of those missing.

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:52.240
There will be some torches missing that when you die and come back,

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:55.520
there will be more torches so that you can get your whip back up to shape.

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:56.880
Oh, interesting. That's cool. That's interesting.

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:58.700
I didn't notice that there were candles missing,

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:04.220
but I will say that a huge improvement in this game with power-ups is that when you die,

00:18:04.420 --> 00:18:09.440
you get the ability to kind of get your whip back up to, you know, to final form real fast.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:13.540
You know, it's usually, like, you'll find the first one kind of, like, right away in your first couple candle hits,

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:18.420
and then maybe if you make it to, like, the next room, you'll be able to get the final form of the whip.

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:22.420
And I like that because if you look at another Konami game like Gradius, it was like,

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:27.180
hey, try and build all this stuff up again before it's too late.

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:28.980
Oh, wait, here's the boss from the end of the stage.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:30.880
It's like, no, that's not how I want to do this.

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:32.000
Yeah, I do think it's cool.

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:37.260
We didn't talk about this, but I think it's cool that your main weapon is upgrade.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.680
Like, you can upgrade your main weapon.

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:40.480
Yeah. I think that's, like, a really interesting thing.

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:42.700
The vampire killer. Oh, that's what it's called.

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:45.440
That's what it's called. The whip is called the vampire killer.

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:50.120
And then for some reason, I don't know why it does it like this,

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:52.700
but the final form is called the morning star.

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:54.620
That's what I was able to find online.

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:56.800
Is that the name of the, like, ball at the end of it?

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:57.800
I think that is what it is.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:01.720
Okay. But, yeah, I just thought that was cool that your main weapon can be upgraded.

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:03.780
Yeah, and it's cool because I don't think we've seen that before.

00:19:03.880 --> 00:19:08.100
Yeah, the original weapon is just, like, a leather whip,

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:10.200
and the ball doesn't come until afterwards.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:12.060
It looks really wimpy in the first form.

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:15.640
Yeah, it's actually. The first form, actually, because I lost it one time,

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:16.900
and it was before I knew about the candles,

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:18.840
so I couldn't find a way to get the whip back.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:20.760
And it was, like, tough to use the real whip.

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:24.280
Yeah, and to Sean's point, it's pathetic, too.

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:25.400
It's, like, weird that this is, like,

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:29.500
this is the great Belmont whip that has been killing vampires for hundreds of years.

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:31.300
Like, I beg to differ.

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:33.560
Does the, like, the basic, basic whip,

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:36.220
does that do less damage, or is it just less reach?

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:37.120
No, it's just less reach.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:38.260
It doesn't do less damage.

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:03.200
Okay, so I think we can talk about bosses a little bit,

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:05.400
and, you know, from there we can talk about stages, too.

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:07.360
So let's just go through stage one.

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:10.060
Which is the Phantom Bat Boss.

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:14.820
What I really like about this level is that you start outside the castle,

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:16.340
you enter your way in,

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:19.180
and then you're just kind of, like, walking through the main hall,

00:20:19.180 --> 00:20:22.380
but there's already, like, some little things here and there

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:26.680
that give you the idea that, like, they put some thought into where enemies were going to be

00:20:26.680 --> 00:20:28.500
and how you would traverse the level.

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:31.080
I really like that you have to go underground

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:33.240
because you can't reach the next set of platforms,

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:35.480
so you have to go under, not underground,

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:37.080
but to the next level of the basement,

00:20:37.520 --> 00:20:42.140
and then venture through to get back up and go over to the next side of the castle.

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:44.060
Like, it's not just a straightforward path.

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:47.140
You mean via, are you talking about just within the first level?

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:48.160
Within the first level, yeah.

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:49.880
Okay. Not when you get to the catacombs.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:51.120
That's cool, but we'll get there.

00:20:51.240 --> 00:20:54.680
Yeah, but even that kind of set the precedent for the rest of the game

00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:55.980
where it's, like, it's side-scrolling,

00:20:55.980 --> 00:21:00.780
but it's not just, like, it's not like Mario where you're just going straight from left to right.

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:05.280
Right. There's a lot of lateral movement and a lot of, like, a little bit of backtracking,

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:07.680
and I can't remember if there's much backtracking in the first level,

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:10.820
but it kind of, like, sets up the idea, like, this is what the game's going to be like.

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:15.740
Well, one thing that I wanted to mention, since you mentioned enemy placement,

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:23.180
and I'm sort of going to crib this point from an old Egoraptor video from, like, seven years ago.

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:31.000
Okay. The way he described it was because of how we have played these side-scrolling action games in the past,

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:33.980
we just sort of just go right.

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:36.380
Go right and, like, hit attack when you see something,

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:41.200
and the enemies are placed in this game so that if you do that, you will just keep dying.

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:45.720
And I love that because I think, you know, one mistake I used to make playing this game

00:21:45.720 --> 00:21:49.860
was just trying to rush through the level, attack what comes at me,

00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:52.860
and it's like, that's not going to work here, especially in the later levels.

00:21:52.860 --> 00:21:57.420
This is a game that wants you to take your time, take a moment, and think about what you're going to do.

00:21:57.820 --> 00:21:59.860
So I really like that about this game.

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:03.780
Yeah, and I also like, you know, I'm not going to say that the enemies are like,

00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:09.320
it's not like Super Mario Bros., where it's designed mechanically to come in on a certain way when you enter the stage,

00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:13.300
but I did appreciate that it wasn't like Kung Fu or Trojan style,

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:16.960
where things just keep continuing to appear and rush into the stage.

00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:18.420
I'm glad it's a Medusa head. Yeah.

00:22:18.660 --> 00:22:20.880
Well, but the Medusa heads do have a method to them, too.

00:22:21.100 --> 00:22:22.540
It's just like where you are.

00:22:22.540 --> 00:22:29.500
Right. But I did notice that sometimes if you defeat something and you go back, it'll be right there again.

00:22:29.800 --> 00:22:31.080
Yeah. If you scroll.

00:22:31.500 --> 00:22:32.440
Yeah, I guess that's what I'm saying.

00:22:32.560 --> 00:22:34.240
It's not like, it's not that polished.

00:22:34.460 --> 00:22:36.060
But it is kind of cool. You know, Super Mario Bros.

00:22:36.220 --> 00:22:37.060
wouldn't let you do that.

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:39.000
That's because you can't go back.

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:40.120
Yeah. Right, right. That's what I'm saying.

00:22:40.780 --> 00:22:41.820
So that's the main hall.

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:43.320
And then you fall into like that.

00:22:43.840 --> 00:22:47.600
What I was trying to say is when you go down to the basement, it's like that where the fishmen come out.

00:22:47.960 --> 00:22:49.080
Oh, I love that part. You know what I'm talking about?

00:22:49.180 --> 00:22:50.120
Those little like. Yeah.

00:22:50.400 --> 00:22:52.560
Now that you mentioned, that's like the only instance of them, right?

00:22:52.580 --> 00:22:53.820
Yeah. That's the only instance of them.

00:22:53.940 --> 00:22:56.000
And at first, I thought they were like incredibly annoying.

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:59.440
But then I realized like, no, just kill them before they ever even like touch ground.

00:22:59.920 --> 00:23:03.520
Yeah. And they shoot like little bubbles and stuff like that.

00:23:03.620 --> 00:23:04.660
But it's really nothing to worry about.

00:23:04.780 --> 00:23:05.680
And you can duck on those.

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:09.980
So I like that. They are, I think, the scariest like designed monster, though.

00:23:10.320 --> 00:23:11.200
Do you think they're the scariest?

00:23:11.260 --> 00:23:14.120
I think so. Not the skeletons that blow their own bones?

00:23:15.240 --> 00:23:19.060
I would say that the fish seem scarier to me than the skeletons.

00:23:19.280 --> 00:23:20.720
Skeletons at this point.

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:28.120
I like the fish. I think that the, maybe not scary, but just the most annoying one where there's a little, what's called the flea guy or something?

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:29.980
Yeah, you want to talk about those guys.

00:23:30.080 --> 00:23:30.940
Oh, I hate those guys.

00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:32.300
And they're not fleas.

00:23:32.440 --> 00:23:35.220
No, no, no. I was watching the speedrunner.

00:23:35.300 --> 00:23:36.160
He called them flea something.

00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:38.400
But they're like frogs, right?

00:23:38.600 --> 00:23:40.020
Yeah, they're little monkey guys.

00:23:40.320 --> 00:23:42.900
They're hunchbacks. Yeah, I forget what they're called.

00:23:42.900 --> 00:23:43.900
They're all of these things.

00:23:44.160 --> 00:23:45.920
But that's like, that's stage three.

00:23:46.220 --> 00:23:48.560
So let's keep going on with stage one here.

00:23:48.720 --> 00:23:51.580
So you get through the fishermen and then the fishermen.

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:53.480
You get through those fish head guys.

00:23:53.900 --> 00:23:56.720
And then you get back up to the main hall again.

00:23:56.720 --> 00:24:02.260
And there's the phantom bat who I thought was just like Dracula in bat form.

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:07.120
Right? Because that's a thing that Dracula does in certain lores that he turns into a bat.

00:24:07.420 --> 00:24:08.820
So I was like, oh, right off the bat.

00:24:08.940 --> 00:24:10.540
Like you're fighting right off the bat.

00:24:10.740 --> 00:24:11.840
You're fighting Dracula.

00:24:11.840 --> 00:24:19.280
Oh. And I thought that was like a cool thing where it's like maybe like Super Mario Brothers where it's like World 1-1, World 1-4.

00:24:19.860 --> 00:24:21.840
And you're fighting Koopa automatically.

00:24:22.160 --> 00:24:23.760
So I presumed it was Dracula.

00:24:23.940 --> 00:24:24.780
Apparently it's not.

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:26.020
It's just a regular bat.

00:24:26.520 --> 00:24:28.900
But Joe, you said that the axe worked out well for you here.

00:24:29.040 --> 00:24:32.220
Yeah, well, it's just because the nature of the bat is flying above your head a lot.

00:24:32.380 --> 00:24:35.600
And you otherwise have to kind of wait for it to get on your level or jump up to it.

00:24:35.660 --> 00:24:37.640
But the axe, you throw in an arc.

00:24:37.860 --> 00:24:40.940
You throw an arc up above your head so you can kind of just keep throwing them up at him.

00:24:40.940 --> 00:24:44.200
And I thought like, oh, the game planned that.

00:24:44.300 --> 00:24:47.840
Yeah. Which is nice. The stopwatch also works on the phantom bat.

00:24:47.860 --> 00:24:51.120
That's how I do. It's a great method because he'll just freeze up.

00:24:51.200 --> 00:24:56.560
And then you can almost whip him and kill him before he unfreezes.

00:24:56.800 --> 00:25:01.600
Wicks back up, yeah. But even if you didn't manage to do that, you just freeze him again and do it all over.

00:25:01.880 --> 00:25:05.660
But I agree that if you don't have the stopwatch at your disposal, the axe is great.

00:25:06.020 --> 00:25:10.480
I don't think that the dagger or the holy water will really help you here.

00:25:10.480 --> 00:25:12.940
Because the holy water definitely won't do it.

00:25:13.880 --> 00:25:15.060
But the phantom bat was cool.

00:25:15.300 --> 00:25:18.580
I liked how it did also when it gets like really close to you.

00:25:18.720 --> 00:25:22.520
If it knows you're in proximity, it kind of does like this psych out charge towards you.

00:25:23.100 --> 00:25:24.820
Where it's not like it's regular movement.

00:25:24.820 --> 00:25:26.980
It moves faster and comes down at you.

00:25:27.120 --> 00:25:30.760
And I thought that was like, wow, it's pretty cool programming that they knew to account for that stuff.

00:25:30.920 --> 00:25:32.540
Yeah, the AI in the game is pretty good.

00:25:32.960 --> 00:25:34.840
For the bosses, I'd say.

00:25:35.080 --> 00:25:39.840
Yeah? Yeah, I don't think the AI for the other enemies has been kind of wonky.

00:25:40.100 --> 00:25:42.640
It's wonky, but I think it's like good enough.

00:25:43.380 --> 00:25:44.300
What's the answer?

00:26:12.020 --> 00:26:16.320
And we can talk about this because now we're moving on to stage two, the torture lab.

00:26:17.200 --> 00:26:18.700
Oh, I didn't know that's what it was called.

00:26:18.960 --> 00:26:20.260
That's what it is.

00:26:20.280 --> 00:26:22.980
And you can kind of see that a little bit, I guess.

00:26:23.100 --> 00:26:25.840
Like there's some skeletal remains and stuff like that.

00:26:26.180 --> 00:26:30.360
But in stage two, that's when you finally meet our skeleton friends who throw their bones.

00:26:30.720 --> 00:26:39.380
And one thing that I like about the AI with them is that at first I was like, no, he's locking himself in a position on the stairs where I can't come up the stairs.

00:26:39.380 --> 00:26:42.740
And now he's just going to be, you know, I'm going to be soft locked out of this.

