01:04:44.240 --> 01:04:46.000
Just stand there. Maybe take a, take a hit or two.

01:04:46.120 --> 01:04:47.560
Oh, okay. But just stand there and throw the holy water.

01:04:47.680 --> 01:04:49.060
Interesting. Yeah.

01:04:49.420 --> 01:04:53.280
Uh, holy water. That's a strategy for the holy water, by the way, of slowing down bosses.

01:04:53.320 --> 01:04:55.340
And we're going to talk about that in a minute, obviously.

01:04:55.700 --> 01:04:59.100
But I, I think that that is, you know, that's a mechanic of the game.

01:04:59.220 --> 01:05:00.040
I don't think it's a mistake.

01:05:00.060 --> 01:05:00.920
I don't think it's a glitch.

01:05:00.920 --> 01:05:03.660
I think they wanted the holy, because you still have to hit them with the whip.

01:05:03.820 --> 01:05:06.540
Correct? No, I think the, and the holy water was just doing the damage, I believe.

01:05:06.540 --> 01:05:07.800
Oh, the holy water's doing the damage, yeah.

01:05:08.060 --> 01:05:11.440
No, I think you're right, because it does it for our, you know, our final boss.

01:05:11.580 --> 01:05:16.020
Yeah. But, um, but I'm kind of shocked, because I gotta go and try that, I guess.

01:05:16.160 --> 01:05:17.960
I, I never had the holy water going into that.

01:05:17.960 --> 01:05:19.060
Yeah, unless they were, because again, I wasn't playing this.

01:05:19.140 --> 01:05:20.580
Maybe they were using the whip, and I just wasn't seeing it.

01:05:20.680 --> 01:05:24.440
Yeah, yeah. I thought they were just going. I was using the boomerang the whole time, but I guess I gotta try my new methods.

01:05:24.440 --> 01:05:25.940
What's happening?

01:05:58.140 --> 01:06:00.300
Anyway, so now we're on Castle Keep,

01:06:00.520 --> 01:06:05.660
and it's crazy because now the first boss of the game is just a regular enemy.

01:06:05.880 --> 01:06:11.600
I know, and you're crossing this broken bridge into the actual Castle Keep, I guess,

01:06:11.740 --> 01:06:15.920
and I'm thinking, oh no, is this just going to be a boss rush?

01:06:16.060 --> 01:06:17.800
Am I going to have to do this all over again?

01:06:18.040 --> 01:06:20.160
And thankfully it's really just that first part of it.

01:06:20.160 --> 01:06:21.680
It's a legitimate concern, though.

01:06:21.720 --> 01:06:25.460
Yeah. Like you see the phantom bat and you're like, well, here we go.

01:06:25.860 --> 01:06:30.380
And then there's like, you know, you're in knockback hell where like these bats are just coming at you.

01:06:30.600 --> 01:06:33.440
I found the best strategy to be is just run past them all.

01:06:33.580 --> 01:06:36.600
Yeah, just dodge them before they can even do the charges and stuff.

01:06:37.020 --> 01:06:40.280
Because then you kind of get into, what is it, like a clock tower?

01:06:40.460 --> 01:06:41.280
Something like that.

01:06:41.540 --> 01:06:43.680
Oh, yeah. It's like a giant gear focused.

01:06:43.860 --> 01:06:44.780
It's like gears and stuff.

01:06:44.920 --> 01:06:50.580
Very weird. But you're going through that and it's not really like, it's not really well designed.

01:06:51.940 --> 01:06:55.800
The clock tower for sure, because there's like weird staircases that lead to nowhere.

01:06:55.940 --> 01:06:59.560
And now the hunchbacks are coming at you from wherever they can.

01:06:59.780 --> 01:07:05.680
It's literally just like, how many enemies can we spam at the, you know, Simon to make sure that he doesn't get to the end?

01:07:05.760 --> 01:07:09.500
I was kind of peeved. I mean, I was able to get through it, but it was annoying.

01:07:10.060 --> 01:07:17.820
So you do, thankfully there's not like much more to go through other than just like, you know, how much can you dodge?

01:07:17.920 --> 01:07:19.120
How much health can you keep?

01:07:19.420 --> 01:07:23.820
Like there's no crazy Medusa head sequence again or anything like that.

01:07:23.880 --> 01:07:28.260
So that's nice. But now we get to our final fight with Dracula.

01:07:28.260 --> 01:07:37.280
And I think it's really cool how they build it up of like, you're basically like going into his bedroom, which is like a coffin in the middle.

01:07:37.720 --> 01:07:42.520
And there's a bunch of candles there to give you some extra stuff, including well-placed holy water.

01:07:43.000 --> 01:07:47.400
And then before you know it, you know, and there's even a music change, which I thought was cool.

01:07:47.540 --> 01:07:50.500
Because it's like unsettling. Usually lines up with some things, yeah.

01:07:50.500 --> 01:08:01.240
And then Dracula appears before you, and he's like, he's able to like teleport, but conveniently wherever you're standing.

01:08:02.060 --> 01:08:08.280
Yeah, it takes a couple, the first couple teleports I think are scripted to specific spaces.

01:08:09.060 --> 01:08:15.500
Because I tried so many times to play this, to fight this boss, that I sort of got like a rhythm to it.

01:08:16.140 --> 01:08:19.020
But never did I beat even this first like form.

01:08:19.760 --> 01:08:27.160
But yeah, after I think like the second or third teleport, it will always be just either on you or right next to you.

01:08:28.100 --> 01:08:31.400
And the interesting thing is that you can only hurt Dracula in the face.

01:08:32.020 --> 01:08:33.560
You have to whip him in the face.

01:08:33.560 --> 01:08:36.040
He's like, he's immune in the body.

01:08:36.040 --> 01:08:38.640
So that's kind of, it's like just a weird thing that you have to do.

01:08:38.840 --> 01:08:44.140
But he's also spitting out like three fireballs out of his cape, whatever comes out of that.

01:08:44.140 --> 01:08:45.680
It's almost like a magic trick.

01:08:46.100 --> 01:08:49.680
You know, he like opens his cape, three fireballs come out.

01:08:50.340 --> 01:08:52.220
Here's my little tip though.

01:08:52.960 --> 01:08:55.960
I was, and I was trying to explain this to Sean, and it's not foolproof.

01:08:56.160 --> 01:08:57.320
You're going to take damage.

01:08:57.620 --> 01:09:01.320
But you want to jump when you see him appear.

01:09:01.520 --> 01:09:06.880
So that when he opens up his cape, the fireballs shoot upwards, aka away from you.

01:09:06.880 --> 01:09:11.440
And then once they've passed you, jump again and hit him in the face.

01:09:12.040 --> 01:09:14.720
And maybe you'll do one brick of damage.

01:09:14.960 --> 01:09:17.040
You know, it's like, you have to do this a lot.

01:09:17.040 --> 01:09:18.580
You're bound to take some damage.

01:09:18.780 --> 01:09:27.300
It's tough. One thing that seemed nice though, was that this is the only boss that if you die, you just get to start right outside of the boss again.

01:09:27.440 --> 01:09:28.980
Yes. You don't have to go through some crazy...

01:09:28.980 --> 01:09:36.940
That's true, and it's kind of weird that they chose to do that, where like as if the Grim Reaper, it's almost like you have to fight another boss sequence.

01:09:37.020 --> 01:09:43.700
I think maybe even they knew that this was like so much harder that like, let's just let people just play it over and over again and see if anyone beats it.

01:09:43.820 --> 01:09:51.920
Well, here's the reason though, I think that they might have done something like that, is because after you take care of, you know, Dracula, we're not done yet.

01:09:51.920 --> 01:09:56.140
That Dracula transforms into what I would describe as like a man bat.

01:09:56.400 --> 01:09:57.720
Let's say a gargoyle almost.

01:09:58.280 --> 01:10:00.840
Yeah, like a gargoyle is a good way of describing it.

01:10:01.100 --> 01:10:05.100
And now it's like, his health goes all the way back up.

01:10:05.100 --> 01:10:06.620
You don't get any extra health.

01:10:06.740 --> 01:10:11.760
And you're like, I gotta fight this giant, like this is massive on the screen.

01:10:11.900 --> 01:10:12.920
Like I can't believe it.

01:10:13.000 --> 01:10:17.000
The sprite work is awesome for this one, given everything that they've already done.

01:10:17.120 --> 01:10:18.740
And now we have space for this guy.

01:10:18.740 --> 01:10:24.620
Like, it's insane, but like, now you can understand why they send you right back to the boss fight.

01:10:24.800 --> 01:10:31.000
Because it's like, well, good luck fighting the whole Dracula fight again if you don't survive this gargoyle man bat fight.

01:10:32.200 --> 01:10:40.740
Yeah, I wish I could have just gotten past the hump of regular humanoid Dracula to play this part.

01:10:40.760 --> 01:10:42.860
Because it seems really memorable.

01:10:43.080 --> 01:10:45.240
But I had to just watch videos of this.

01:10:45.240 --> 01:10:49.640
Yeah, the reason I wasn't talking for so long was because I was dead long before all of this.

01:10:51.000 --> 01:10:54.320
The interesting thing here though is that man bat doesn't live up to the hype.

01:10:54.600 --> 01:11:02.100
Because that holy water that you were able to get through one of the candles in the last room is now like the most effective method to stopping him.

01:11:02.160 --> 01:11:03.600
So just make sure you've got hearts.

01:11:03.780 --> 01:11:07.340
And remember, it only takes one heart to use the holy water.

01:11:07.600 --> 01:11:09.360
So just have a bunch of hearts stocked up.

01:11:09.500 --> 01:11:10.580
Throw that holy water.

01:11:10.580 --> 01:11:12.860
It'll do massive damage to him.

01:11:12.980 --> 01:11:15.620
It'll also freeze him in his place so you can whip him.

01:11:15.880 --> 01:11:19.380
He does have a weak spot where the face does the most damage.

01:11:19.380 --> 01:11:22.600
So I do think that's kind of cool as like a boss with a weak spot.

01:11:22.820 --> 01:11:25.680
Similar to how like the axe knight had that back of the head thing.

01:11:27.320 --> 01:11:30.660
And, you know, just take that all the way to the bank.

01:11:30.840 --> 01:11:33.800
Don't try and get funny here unless you're really good at the game.

01:11:34.320 --> 01:11:38.420
Because you're most likely not going to make it through this fight if you don't spam the holy water.

01:11:38.520 --> 01:11:39.520
Which makes sense, right?

01:11:39.520 --> 01:11:42.420
Right? Wouldn't you finish off Dracula with the holy water?

01:11:42.600 --> 01:11:45.980
Yeah. Like after a while, it's not like the physical damage.

01:11:45.980 --> 01:11:48.720
It's the magic that's really doing the work.

01:11:49.000 --> 01:11:55.300
And so you destroy, you defeat Dracula, you destroy the castle, and then you find out it was all a movie.

01:11:57.520 --> 01:11:58.820
Played by. Yeah.

01:11:58.940 --> 01:12:00.360
I have the cast pulled up.

01:12:00.460 --> 01:12:01.300
Oh, you have the cast?

01:12:01.300 --> 01:12:03.000
Please tell us. I love this.

01:12:03.000 --> 01:12:05.480
Who is the cast? Dracula was Christopher B.

01:12:06.360 --> 01:12:07.240
Christopher B.

01:12:07.240 --> 01:12:09.600
Yeah. No relation to Christopher Lee.

01:12:09.920 --> 01:12:13.140
Yeah. Keep going. Death was Bela Lugosi.

01:12:13.600 --> 01:12:15.140
No relation to Bela Lugosi.

01:12:15.440 --> 01:12:18.740
Yes. Frankenstein was Boris Karloffis.

01:12:19.140 --> 01:12:20.800
What's crazier though, can we talk about this?

01:12:20.940 --> 01:12:22.240
This isn't even clever.

01:12:22.640 --> 01:12:24.900
It's just they just changed like one letter.

01:12:25.140 --> 01:12:30.100
You know? I think it was Angry Video Game Nerd who did something where he was like, that's like if

01:12:30.100 --> 01:12:33.420
I change Steven Spielberg to Steven Bielberg.

01:12:33.780 --> 01:12:35.680
You know? That was exactly what it was.

01:12:35.680 --> 01:12:36.660
It's not funny.

01:12:38.620 --> 01:12:40.620
It's just like, we don't want to be in trouble.

01:12:40.780 --> 01:12:45.060
But we also want to pay homage to all of these original people who played all these parts.

01:12:45.860 --> 01:12:46.780
It was cute. Yeah.

01:12:46.820 --> 01:12:47.700
I thought it was really cute.

01:12:47.700 --> 01:12:51.580
I like the idea that it's a movie because it helps the idea that it's all just a universal

01:12:51.580 --> 01:12:57.420
tour too. Well also something, again, I didn't play this part, but the Let's Players called this out.

01:12:57.780 --> 01:13:00.040
You're still in the castle when it collapses.

01:13:01.700 --> 01:13:03.660
You just see like a shot.

01:13:03.800 --> 01:13:05.360
That happens later.

01:13:05.660 --> 01:13:06.520
Simon's still in there.

01:13:06.580 --> 01:13:07.720
That just happens later though.

01:13:08.000 --> 01:13:09.080
You don't see the time.

01:13:09.220 --> 01:13:10.040
The time is skip. Yeah.

01:13:10.260 --> 01:13:11.120
It happens at night.

01:13:11.120 --> 01:13:12.760
Yeah. With the illusion of film.

01:13:13.220 --> 01:13:14.300
You left and now it's morning.

01:13:14.840 --> 01:13:17.160
Because it's a film, you know, it's just a cut.

01:13:17.300 --> 01:13:19.180
Did your actions even cause that to happen?

01:13:19.640 --> 01:13:20.820
Did your actions even cause...

01:13:20.820 --> 01:13:22.740
It might have been the townsfolk, you know?

01:13:22.800 --> 01:13:25.040
Maybe it was just going to collapse that day anyway.

01:13:25.160 --> 01:13:26.100
You didn't even have to go in there.

01:13:26.360 --> 01:13:28.640
Some fault activity in Transylvania that day.

01:13:28.860 --> 01:13:29.760
So it was all moot.

01:13:29.820 --> 01:13:31.340
So I imagine Simon's just kicking himself.

01:13:31.460 --> 01:13:34.840
It's like, I could have just waited another day and the castle would just collapse.

01:13:35.180 --> 01:13:36.980
Do we want to read the rest of them or no?

01:13:37.120 --> 01:13:40.860
No, I think we're good. I want to add one more.

01:13:41.000 --> 01:13:45.520
Sure. Your character, the hero, the actor's name is Simon Belmondo.

01:13:45.700 --> 01:13:46.740
Yeah, Belmondo.

01:13:47.200 --> 01:13:50.540
Which is actually what he goes by in the Japanese games.

01:13:50.840 --> 01:13:51.780
Not Belmondo.

01:13:51.900 --> 01:13:54.880
Belmondo. Which I think is a really strange choice.

01:13:55.340 --> 01:13:56.640
I don't know if the...

01:13:56.640 --> 01:13:57.620
You know... He sounds bigger.

01:13:57.860 --> 01:14:00.060
Yeah, yeah, yeah. He sounds Belmondo.

01:14:01.340 --> 01:14:02.940
So there's that whole...

01:14:02.940 --> 01:14:04.040
It's a movie thing.

01:14:04.180 --> 01:14:05.080
Which I don't mind at all.

01:14:05.320 --> 01:14:08.740
What bothers me is that then you get dropped right back into stage one.

01:14:08.740 --> 01:14:11.480
But it is a harder version of the game.

01:14:11.880 --> 01:14:14.620
And so it's like one thing I'm fine with it all being a movie.

01:14:14.820 --> 01:14:17.720
But then you get dropped right back into stage one again.

01:14:17.960 --> 01:14:19.520
And you would just think like, oh, that's okay.

01:14:19.580 --> 01:14:20.600
I just got to play the whole game again.

01:14:20.680 --> 01:14:23.420
But you don't realize it's a harder version of the game.

01:14:23.500 --> 01:14:26.980
Oh, really? It is a hard mode inside the hard difficulty already.

01:14:27.340 --> 01:14:29.320
Which is strange because who...

01:14:29.320 --> 01:14:32.420
Okay. I know this game doesn't have a save function.

01:14:32.660 --> 01:14:33.840
At least in the NES version.

01:14:34.280 --> 01:14:37.520
But who has time in the day to play this game twice?

01:14:37.900 --> 01:14:39.300
Without being able to shut it off.

01:14:39.500 --> 01:14:41.600
Yeah. You must keep it on.

01:14:41.620 --> 01:14:42.420
You gotta leave it on overnight.

01:14:42.560 --> 01:14:44.820
And you know your dad's gonna be like, turn that thing off.

01:14:45.440 --> 01:14:46.780
We got bills to pay.

01:14:47.000 --> 01:14:50.180
But it's interesting because it is just a little more than just being harder.

01:14:50.360 --> 01:14:53.740
It's also like different items change and stuff like that too.

01:14:53.860 --> 01:14:54.820
There's different...

01:14:54.820 --> 01:14:56.620
Different secrets for the food, right?

01:14:56.620 --> 01:14:58.380
Different secrets for the food and stuff like that.

01:14:58.380 --> 01:15:01.580
And something that we haven't talked about yet, but I think is worth talking about now,

01:15:01.720 --> 01:15:05.920
is that you get rewarded for doing the weirdest things in this game, okay?

01:15:06.620 --> 01:15:09.520
Walking certain ways gets you prizes.

01:15:10.280 --> 01:15:12.800
Standing in certain places gets you prizes.

01:15:13.440 --> 01:15:15.500
Hitting certain walls gives you prizes.

01:15:15.580 --> 01:15:17.240
There are prizes that you guys didn't even know about.

01:15:17.440 --> 01:15:18.640
There are treasure chests.

01:15:19.000 --> 01:15:21.020
There are crowns. There's a treasure chest?

01:15:21.040 --> 01:15:21.940
There's a treasure chest.

01:15:22.080 --> 01:15:23.120
There are crowns.

01:15:23.500 --> 01:15:24.560
There's a...

01:15:24.560 --> 01:15:26.180
Just to give you an easy example of this.

01:15:26.180 --> 01:15:31.980
You know, in the very first level, when you're back outside of the castle, as you walk towards

01:15:31.980 --> 01:15:35.480
the entrance, you are forced in to walk through the entrance.

01:15:35.520 --> 01:15:41.280
If you manage to jump over the part that would force the cutscene and stand over by the castle

01:15:41.280 --> 01:15:44.220
and just stand there, a bag of money will just drop.

01:15:45.380 --> 01:15:49.480
And then you can go jump back over the cutscene again and collect the bag of money.

01:15:49.700 --> 01:15:51.040
That's how these things work.

01:15:51.180 --> 01:16:00.100
But sometimes it's like you also have to be pushing up against the wall as if it was pushing a hidden block or something to have something fall out.

01:16:00.100 --> 01:16:03.360
So that's where things like treasure chest, crowns show up.

01:16:03.520 --> 01:16:05.260
But here comes the crazy part, okay?

01:16:06.440 --> 01:16:11.880
And in the second, you know, if you beat the whole game and do it the second time, even though they're in different locations,

01:16:12.380 --> 01:16:17.080
now some really funny things start to show up, like Moai Islands.

01:16:17.640 --> 01:16:18.560
The Moai heads.

01:16:18.660 --> 01:16:21.040
Are you serious? From Gradius, yes.

01:16:21.040 --> 01:16:25.280
From where? The Moai heads, they just drop when you stand in certain positions.

01:16:25.480 --> 01:16:26.500
Do they drop on you?

01:16:26.640 --> 01:16:28.320
No, no, no, no. They drop as a collectible.

01:16:28.420 --> 01:16:29.560
They're worth 4,000 points.

01:16:29.560 --> 01:16:34.400
That's an interesting, like, I feel like there's some theory, some shared universe theory there.

01:16:34.620 --> 01:16:38.180
Those Moai heads, man, they won't, the Easter Island guys, they won't leave.

01:16:38.280 --> 01:16:39.140
That's a real Easter egg.

01:16:39.340 --> 01:16:40.260
What's with Konami in this stuff?

01:16:40.260 --> 01:16:41.280
I don't know. They love it.

01:16:41.760 --> 01:16:46.120
But, yeah, I just think that's so cool that there's, like, a, you know, like, fun with pose.

01:16:46.260 --> 01:16:48.200
And, you know, it's like stuff that you couldn't even get your friends to believe.

01:16:48.300 --> 01:16:55.340
It's like, yeah, you just gotta destroy that one rock, and then you can jump down to that platform that seemed like you couldn't go on that platform.

01:16:55.400 --> 01:16:58.060
And if you just wait there, a bag of money will drop.

01:16:58.060 --> 01:17:00.160
That sounds like he strikes a pose?

01:17:00.280 --> 01:17:02.060
Like you said, like, a pose? He doesn't strike a pose.

01:17:02.240 --> 01:17:06.540
Oh, okay. It's posing in the sense of, like, they want you to be in that specific spot.

01:17:06.560 --> 01:17:08.260
You have to be in that pose.

01:17:08.340 --> 01:17:13.200
I wonder if any of this is, like, debug stuff where they need to test the items in certain places.

01:17:13.200 --> 01:17:15.960
And they're like, all right, well, I'll just do this obscure thing, and then it'll just happen.

01:17:15.980 --> 01:17:21.680
But this is the only way to get treasure chests and crowns and the moa island.

01:17:21.680 --> 01:17:23.500
Yeah, I think that debunks that, yeah.

01:17:23.720 --> 01:17:24.640
Yeah, it's...

01:17:24.640 --> 01:17:26.800
Not these, but, like, the other ones.

01:17:27.140 --> 01:17:28.900
You know, like, the other weird things.

01:17:29.060 --> 01:17:30.220
Not, like, for the hard playthrough.

01:17:30.220 --> 01:17:31.860
But I do think, I think it's intentional.

01:17:32.040 --> 01:17:37.340
I think the whole game is filled with these kinds of secrets, similar to how, like, the game never tells you to smash the wall.

01:17:37.340 --> 01:17:40.340
But then one time you accidentally do it and find food.

01:17:40.340 --> 01:17:41.960
Now you're going to be smashing every wall.

01:17:42.060 --> 01:17:45.000
Yeah. If you're a kid, you're going to be looking for everything, right?

01:17:45.180 --> 01:17:47.580
Yeah. So I think that's a really nice touch.

01:17:47.980 --> 01:17:54.920
And it's kind of cool to see another game that we love so much getting put into this game in some way or another.

01:17:54.920 --> 01:17:58.080
Even though maybe we didn't like to deal with them in that game.

01:17:58.460 --> 01:18:18.000
Right. So now we have to talk about the music, guys.

01:18:18.220 --> 01:18:22.540
Okay? Because everybody should be in love with this music.

01:18:22.540 --> 01:18:25.440
But it is, like, revered in terms of video game music.

01:18:25.460 --> 01:18:27.540
It gets made over and over and over again.

01:18:27.760 --> 01:18:35.180
