And now, just to touch on something.

01:26:59.180 --> 01:27:01.240
So, there are different versions of this game.

01:27:01.240 --> 01:27:05.120
And I'm not just talking about MSX and Game Boy and stuff like that.

01:27:05.600 --> 01:27:12.360
These are real different versions in the sense that Akumazu Dracula is what it's called in Japan.

01:27:12.360 --> 01:27:17.320
And I think that just stands for Dracula's Castle or something like that.

01:27:17.400 --> 01:27:19.200
It's not directly Castlevania.

01:27:19.320 --> 01:27:20.300
We get Castlevania.

01:27:20.300 --> 01:27:21.740
They get Akumazu Dracula.

01:27:22.300 --> 01:27:26.100
And the Famicom Disk System version comes out first in 86.

01:27:26.100 --> 01:27:32.120
And the only difference really there, besides a couple of balancing things, is that you can save your game.

01:27:32.280 --> 01:27:33.100
You can save your game.

01:27:33.100 --> 01:27:39.500
You can name your character file so that at the end with the movie sequence, it'll name you as Simon Belmondo.

01:27:39.500 --> 01:27:42.400
Belmondo. Which is his name in Japan.

01:27:43.060 --> 01:27:51.240
And then, weirdly enough, sometime in the 90s, the Famicom got the cartridge version of Castlevania.

01:27:51.320 --> 01:27:54.320
So, they already had the disk version, but they're like, oh, maybe you guys want the cartridge version.

01:27:54.320 --> 01:27:57.980
However, they added an easy mode to it.

01:27:58.140 --> 01:28:00.240
Like, an actual selectable at the main menu.

01:28:00.340 --> 01:28:02.940
You can select hard or easy.

01:28:03.100 --> 01:28:03.920
No normal mode.

01:28:04.340 --> 01:28:07.080
And easy makes it so that you start with 30 hearts.

01:28:07.080 --> 01:28:08.320
You have 9 lives.

01:28:08.460 --> 01:28:09.740
You take less damage.

01:28:10.060 --> 01:28:13.880
Your double and triple shots retain when picking up different sub-weapons.

01:28:14.260 --> 01:28:17.940
And, you're not going to believe this, no knockback.

01:28:18.460 --> 01:28:23.320
What? They got rid of knockback in the easy mode of...

