01:28:33.600 --> 01:28:34.780
They still stun you.

01:28:34.920 --> 01:28:41.380
It's not like you can do, like, invincibility hits and, like, just walk through enemies and then walk through a few while you have your temporary invincibility.

01:28:41.560 --> 01:28:42.580
They do stun you.

01:28:42.740 --> 01:28:44.520
You just don't go flying backwards.

01:28:44.520 --> 01:28:54.960
I want to know, though, like, in the context of the early 90s when this game came out, was there an argument among fans about just, like, the get good, play the hard mode?

01:28:55.260 --> 01:28:58.160
Or were there people that were like, oh, no, no, you can play the easy mode?

01:28:58.160 --> 01:28:59.880
I'm sure people are going to argue about everything.

01:29:00.100 --> 01:29:05.120
Yeah. And to be fair, though, you know, us North Americans, we never knew how hard we had it.

01:29:05.320 --> 01:29:07.320
Yeah. They just gave us harder games.

01:29:07.660 --> 01:29:16.120
Both the Famicom Disk System version and the cartridge version are easier than the version we got, maybe because they just wanted us to stay with the game longer.

01:29:16.340 --> 01:29:17.220
Which wouldn't make sense.

01:29:17.660 --> 01:29:25.660
Although, for speedrunning, the knockback is actually really important because there are some jumps that you can't make in the normal game that you use.

01:29:25.740 --> 01:29:29.940
You bounce off of enemies using the knockback to reach higher platforms.

01:29:30.220 --> 01:29:34.060
Wow. It's, like, a main strategy in speedrunning, like, skipping staircases that way.

01:29:34.060 --> 01:29:37.480
Okay. And there's even one section where you just skip an entire section.

01:29:38.020 --> 01:29:40.380
Just using the knockback from a bat or something.

01:29:40.740 --> 01:29:42.940
Wow. Yeah. Okay.

01:29:43.120 --> 01:29:46.440
I mean, that was, you know, like, for me, I love that easy mode.

01:29:46.440 --> 01:29:49.660
I'm not ashamed to say that that's how I beat the game and played through it.

01:29:49.680 --> 01:29:50.800
